  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Sewn on both sides of single back board with text on left and illustrations on right. Each page opens using alternating spines as hinge point, overlaying pages on top of each other. Book housed in paper sleeve. Poem printed letterpress in Adobe Jensen. Reproductions of Monet's paintings printed offset.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The text appears on thin Japanese paper that obscures yet hints at a painting beneath. Turning each text page to the left reveals richly colored details of one of six Monet paintings. Turning the image to the right presents the reader with more text. Words and images intermingle and alternate until the final page: a stunning image of one of Monet's late water lily paintings." --Artist's statement.</subfield>
  </datafield>
